Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "Github: https://github.com/AuroraDysis/KerrP2P\n\nKerrP2P is a software \
designed for forward ray tracing in Kerr spacetime. It is specifically \
tailored to efficiently calculate multiple null geodesics between designated \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]source\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] points, locate \
apparent positions of the corresponding images, and quantify their shapes. \
Detailed information can be found in the paper ",
 ButtonBox["Forward Ray Tracing and Hot Spots in Kerr Spacetime",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.111.064075"], 
    None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.111.064075"],
 " by Lihang Zhou, Zhen Zhong, Yifan Chen, and Vitor Cardoso.\n\nThis \
software contains a Python/C++ part and a Mathematica part. The Python/C++ \
part is aimed at high-precision contour plot calculation to locate the \
multiple images. The Mathematica part (i.e., this notebook) takes the \
conserved quantities generated by the former as input, visualizes the \
geodesics in 3D, and calculates the positions and shapes of the resulting \
images."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.953561430471484*^9, 3.953561434348343*^9}, 
   3.95356147027922*^9, {3.9535615029063797`*^9, 3.95356153794906*^9}, {
   3.9535616159828367`*^9, 3.953561659372547*^9}, {3.953561738255229*^9, 
   3.953561741687731*^9}, {3.9535617931973124`*^9, 3.9535619801272917`*^9}, {
